"cascade", "entities": [1017, 1593], "window": [42136, 80535], "confidence": 0.91, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Under the 600-unit max-wait rule, 1017's temporal forward-set is only 22 nodes and excludes 1593; path enumeration yields nothing. The connection that exists when waiting is unbounded relies on hop gaps of 3105-12524 units, notably a 12524-unit gap before the terminal 603->1593 contact at t=78011, so influence could not have been carried. Both endpoints are active and statically well-connected via hubs 319/596, and there is no direct edge, confirming the negative reflects temporal discontinuity rather than sparse activity or missing structure. Relaxations to 1500 and 3000 still fail, showing robustness."}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion: no genuine cascade.**\n\nKey findings:\n- With the 600-unit constraint, 1017 reaches only 22 nodes and never 1593 (step_01); enumeration returns zero paths (step_06).\n- A time-respecting path *does* exist if waiting is unconstrained (step_03), but its inter-hop gaps are 3105, 5302, 9045, 375, 12524 \u2014 four of five hops exceed the budget by 5\u201320\u00d7. All five enumerated routes (step_13) funnel through the same late `142\u2192603 @65487 \u2192 603\u21921593 @78011` tail, a 12,524-unit dormancy.\n- Relaxing the threshold to 1500 and 3000 still fails (step_09, step_10), so the negative isn't a knife-edge artifact.\n- Confounder controls: both endpoints are genuinely active (22 and 19 events, step_05) and the static 2-hop neighbourhood is dense (step_04), so \"no activity\" or \"no structural connection\" cannot explain the result \u2014 this is specifically a *timing* failure. Intermediaries include hubs like 319 (213 events) and 596 (99 events) (step_11), whose popularity creates static paths without temporal continuity. There is no direct edge (step_12). 1017 cannot even reach the penultimate node 603 under the constraint (step_14). The 1593-side activity is back-loaded into the final bin (step_15), long after 1017's early activity.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_85c5e4e7\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1017, 1593],\n  \"window\": [42136, 80535],\n  \"confidence\": 0.91,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Under the 600-unit max-wait rule, 1017's temporal forward-set is only 22 nodes and excludes 1593; path enumeration yields nothing. The connection that exists when waiting is unbounded relies on hop gaps of 3105-12524 units, notably a 12524-unit gap before the terminal 603->1593 contact at t=78011, so influence could not have been carried. Both endpoints are active and statically well-connected via hubs 319/596, and there is no direct edge, confirming the negative reflects temporal discontinuity rather than sparse activity or missing structure. Relaxations to 1500 and 3000 still fail, showing robustness.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 52035, "total_output_tokens": 3937, "total_tokens": 55972, "total_latency_ms": 58540, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}